  "notes": "West's club opening lead is won by South with the ♣A. The hand is solid except for the ♠Q. South must avoid losing 2 trump tricks to make the slam.\n\nIf the contract was 7 spades it would be correct to cross to the dummy and finesse East for the ♠Q (\"8 ever\". This would be a poor play in a small slam as West could win the ♠Q and give East a ruff in the red suit that South crossed to dummy in.\n\nAn alternative is to cash the ♠A and ♠K and use the ♠J or ♠10 to drive out the ♠Q. The problem with this line is that if a defender was dealt 4 trumps, he will play a red suit after winning the ♠Q. South will be unable to return to his hand to draw trump and the defense might be able to ruff 1 of dummy's top winners.\n\nThe solution is to lead the ♠J or ♠10 immediately. If a defender holding 4 spades to the ♠Q ducks, South can simply cash the ♠A and ♠K. The defense will be held to one trump trick.\n\nIf the defense wins the ♠Q and plays a red suit, South can win in dummy. Dummy's remaining small trump provides a safe link to the South hand to draw the outstanding trumps.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West's club opening lead is won by South with the ♣A. The hand is solid except for the ♠Q. South must avoid losing 2 trump tricks to make the slam.",
    "If the contract was 7 spades it would be correct to cross to the dummy and finesse East for the ♠Q (\"8 ever\". This would be a poor play in a small slam as West could win the ♠Q and give East a ruff in the red suit that South crossed to dummy in.",
    "An alternative is to cash the ♠A and ♠K and use the ♠J or ♠10 to drive out the ♠Q. The problem with this line is that if a defender was dealt 4 trumps, he will play a red suit after winning the ♠Q. South will be unable to return to his hand to draw trump and the defense might be able to ruff 1 of dummy's top winners.",
    "The solution is to lead the ♠J or ♠10 immediately. If a defender holding 4 spades to the ♠Q ducks, South can simply cash the ♠A and ♠K. The defense will be held to one trump trick.",
    "If the defense wins the ♠Q and plays a red suit, South can win in dummy. Dummy's remaining small trump provides a safe link to the South hand to draw the outstanding trumps."
